# The escalator, a lift bar that rides back and forth (Escalator.java): native 32x8 frames, hand-typed (#236, replacing the
# inherited grey bar with no source). Exported by tools/export_object_sprites.py (export_escalators): frame off is
# assets/images/objects/GreyOff.png, frames on1..on8 are GreyOn.png (one row), both with the moon rim (D92).
# Active family (ART_DIRECTION colour by meaning, "Mechanisms"): the top row, the part you stand on, is the walk cue straw
# `e1cfa5` in both states. Stopped (off): a dull steel body with four bolts and the hub's blade upright in steel. Running
# (on1..on8): the body is a dark belt with straw-shade `c4b07e` chevrons (period 8 px) that move 1 px per frame toward the
# way the bar travels (Escalator mirrors the frame with its direction), and the hub's blade, in straw, turns an eighth of
# a turn per frame round its lit boss: a single frame reads as running at play scale. Row 2 is the bar's top, rows 3-5
# its body, row 6 its ink underside, row 7 the axle bracket.
size 32 8
color k 211f30
color S e1cfa5
color s c4b07e
color m 858d99
color g 62677a
color a afbbc3
color d 48475b
color H 35334a
frame off
